# Line-by-line notes: lines starting with # are comments. Docker ignores them.
# What this file does:
#   Lists files and folders Docker must NOT copy into the image.
#   Keeps the image small and keeps secrets and Windows-only files out of it.
#   Each non-comment line is a path pattern. Comments must be on their own line.

# Local virtual environment (Windows-specific, not needed in the container). Skips the whole .venv folder.
.venv
# Python cache folders. ** means "any folder at any depth".
**/__pycache__
# Pytest's cache folder.
.pytest_cache
# Local secrets file. The container gets its settings from docker-compose.yml instead.
.env
# This file list and the Dockerfile are not needed inside the image.
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
# Test code is not needed to run the API.
tests
